 the  settlements are and they have said you  know that they have made a lot of  pressure Netanyahu to annex this  territory now the Palestinians are very  much concerned that all of this together  might set you know the atmosphere also  seeing that there was a very muted  international reaction there has been a  lot of criticism but it was a muted  reaction more or less that you know they  might go ahead with their with these  plans you know just just days before the  general election I have to assume there  are some people who might view this as a  blatant appeal to amass non-arab votes  is Netanyahu feeling pressure well this  is certainly welling cry out which to  his most nationalist base and he wants  to tell his voters to go out and vote  for Likud or reaching out to those  voters who are thinking about voting for  the smaller some of the smaller  right-wing and ultra nationalist parties  there are a lot of them wanting as seats  in the Knesset and some of them might  not come over at the election special so  every vote to those parties might be a  lost vote for Netanyahu but he's also  under pressure because there has been a  tight race between the Likud his party  and the newly formed blue-and-white  party by the former army achieved penny  guns and pulses predict a neck-to-neck a  race having said that in Israeli  politics it's all about being able to  form a coalition and he opposes again  predict and we have to take those polls  of course with the grain of soul they're  not always that accurate but that  Netanyahu has much more chances to find  partners and to form a coalition within  his right wing bloc than a mr. guns now  having said that these are the parties  the smaller right wing ultra nationalist  parties that have a Pro annexation  agenda and they might actually ask him  for Christ to turn his coalition ask him  to follow up on this election Platt  Tanya Kramer in Jerusalem for DW thanks  so much for joining us  you
 

